# MUON backend env.
#
# LOCAL-FIRST / EMBEDDED (the default, per docs/adr/0008): leave DATABASE_URL
# UNSET. The backend then computes `file:<dataDir>/muon.db` (per-user SQLite,
# loopback bind, auto local token, lockfile) and "just works", no server, no
# token to configure. `npm run dev` in backend with the vars below UNSET runs
# the embedded brain. (A stale `postgresql://` DATABASE_URL here while the schema
# is on the sqlite provider will fail to boot, review finding F6.)
#
# HOSTED ("Team/Cloud"): set DATABASE_URL to Postgres AND swap the schema's
# datasource `provider = "sqlite"` → `"postgresql"` (one line, see the comment
# atop prisma/schema.prisma), then set MUON_API_TOKEN.

# PORT=4000                    # hosted only; embedded binds 127.0.0.1:0
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/muon
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3050
# MUON_API_TOKEN=your-secret-token-min-8-chars   # hosted only; embedded mints one

# Optional (embedded or hosted):
# MUON_DATA_DIR=                # override the per-user data dir
# MUON_GRAPH_DIR=.muon/graph
# MUON_GRAPH_DISABLE_FTS=0      # 1 where the Ladybug FTS native ext can't load
